---
title: Sequence Translation
sidebar:
  order: 19
---

Translate DNA sequences to amino acid sequences.

## Example

```python
import pysegul

def translate_sequences():
    translate = pysegul.SequenceTranslation(
        input_fmt='nexus',
        datatype='dna',
        output_path='tests/output',
        output_format='fasta',
        table='1',
        reading_frame=1,
        )
    translate.from_dir('tests/align-data')
```

To use a list of files, call `from_files` instead of `from_dir`:

```python
translate.from_files(['tests/align-data/alignment1.nex', 'tests/align-data/alignment2.nex'])
```

## Options

| Option | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `input_fmt` | Required | `'auto'`, `'fasta'`, `'nexus'`, `'phylip'` |
| `datatype` | Required | `'dna'`, `'aa'`, `'ignore'` |
| `output_path` | Required | Output directory |
| `output_format` | Required | `'fasta'`, `'nexus'`, `'phylip'`, or interleaved `'fasta-int'`, `'nexus-int'`, `'phylip-int'` |
| `table` | `'1'` | NCBI genetic code number as a string. See [supported translation tables](/docs/cli-usage/sequence-translate/#supported-translation-tables) |
| `reading_frame` | `None` | `1`, `2`, or `3`. Detected for each file when not set |

## Methods

| Method | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `from_dir(input_dir)` | Translate the sequence files in a directory |
| `from_files(input_files)` | Translate a list of sequence files |
